
# MachSig census artifacts: 17MB JSONL, regenerated by `python3 tools/machsig/regen.py` at any commit.
# NOT ~5s, as this note said until 2026-10-13: extract.lean takes ~8.5 min on this machine (measured
# 2026-10-13, both 23e0d047 and c3046961), extract_statement.lean ~20 s. Storing the outputs would add
# ~40MB per regeneration to git history; the extractor is the artifact, the census is its output.
# Because the signature set is NOT in git, it carries its own source identity (first JSONL record;
# tools/machsig/identity.py) and the trust gate refuses a set whose identity is not this tree's.
artifacts/machsig_extraction.json
artifacts/machsig_trust_raw.tsv
artifacts/machsig_trust.err
artifacts/machsig_build.log
artifacts/machsig_build.log.err
artifacts/*.tmp
artifacts/machsig_raw.tsv
artifacts/machsig_raw.err
artifacts/machsig_census.jsonl
artifacts/machsig_census.csv
artifacts/machsig_terms_raw.tsv
artifacts/machsig_terms.err
artifacts/machsig_terms.jsonl
artifacts/machsig_stmt_raw.tsv
artifacts/machsig_stmt.err
artifacts/machsig_stability_cases.jsonl
artifacts/machsig_signatures.jsonl
